# {{ service_name }}

A local Pokerlost FastAPI foundation. It provides health, canonical root/OpenAPI infrastructure, and fail-closed authorization support; no business operation is implemented.

## 🚀 Run

Python 3.14+ and access to the pinned private `pypokerlost` source are required to install. The installed wheel includes the SDK as a runtime dependency; it does not need an adjacent checkout. No database URL or outbound credential is needed for this default render.

```bash
uv lock
uv sync --locked
make run
```

`GET /` uses `PokerlostResponse[None]`; `GET /getOpenApi` returns the unmodified OpenAPI document. `/health/live` and `/health/ready` are infrastructure probes. Read `SERVICE.md` for this service's data boundary, [architecture](docs/architecture.md) for the foundation lifecycle, and `AGENTS.md` for local work rules. {% if withTesting %}Run `make test-unit` for isolated coverage and `make test` for all enabled capabilities. A DB render requires a disposable `TEST_DATABASE_URL`.{% endif %} {% if withCi %}CI checks source without a secret on PRs; a private SDK build requires a reviewed SHA and an approved, narrowly scoped App installation.{% endif %}

## 📦 Container and deployment candidate

`make ci-local` runs applicable checks once; `make version` and
`make release-check` read and validate artifact versions. Wheel, sdist and chart
share `dist/<source-content-sha256>/`, preserving previous rollback artifacts.
After a successful online run, `make ci-local OFFLINE=1` validates prepared
SDK/build/database inputs and runs fresh acceptance without fetching dependencies.

{% if withDocker %}`make check build image verify` uses the inherited multi-stage build and fresh
installed-wheel tests. Private SDK installation requires a short-lived SDK-only read token through
`DOCKER_BUILD_ARGS='--secret id=sdk_token,env=SDK_APP_TOKEN'` after owner/full-SHA admission. Neither a
credential nor a development tool is copied into the runtime. The final process runs as UID 65532
and supports a read-only filesystem and graceful SIGTERM.
{% endif %}{% if withKubernetes %}`make chart` packages the managed chart, `make chart-check` validates it,
and `make deploy-local` / `make undeploy-local` operate this application's disposable Kind cluster.
`deploy/values.yaml` belongs to the application; `deploy/chart/` follows the shared template.
External deployment requires a tested image manifest digest and an approved target.
{% endif %}

Ordinary PR CI has no SDK secret and does not verify B1. Private checks use owner-only manual dispatch (actor and triggering actor serrja), full SHA equal to the branch SHA and `SDK_BUILD_REVIEWED_SHA`, and the existing SDK-only App. The owner must provision repository secrets and activate the CI-only workflow registration. This is an accepted solo-writer policy, not a reviewer-protected environment. A skipped private job fails manual acceptance. Coverage percentages are advisory; test, build, type, configuration and report errors fail. Workflow artifacts and BuildKit caches stay within the
private repository; no image, package or release is published by these commands.

